Thus plan: For origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha:

1. Prepare each (confirm_candidate_preparedness) after attaching task profile and ensuring vehicle allocated (they already have vehicle allocated). So steps: attach_task_profile, then confirm_candidate_preparedness.

2. Assign operator resource (assign_operator_resource) to each.

3. Activate node (activate_origin_node / activate_destination_node) to make node ready.

4. Lock origin/destination availability (lock_origin_availability / lock_destination_availability) to get locked and confirmed.

5. Assemble transport leg (assemble_transport_leg) using the locked availabilities, nodes ready, transport leg available.

6. Authorize transport leg loading (authorize_transport_leg_loading) using origin_availability (needs task profile linked) - we have that.

7. Mark origin availability dispatch ready (mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready) and mark destination availability dispatch ready (mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready) - each requires lock, confirmed, leg assembled, loading authorized.

8. Allocate dispatch slot for each (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate) using dispatch_ready and available slot.

9. Execute dispatch for each (execute_origin_dispatch for origin, execute_destination_dispatch for destination) to set dispatched and free vehicle.

10. Load payload onto origin and destination (load_origin_payload, load_destination_payload) to occupy nodes and link payload.

